# Overrides the root .dockerignore for this specific Dockerfile (same
# directory as the Dockerfile itself — BuildKit's documented convention
# since Docker Engine 23.0). The root one has a bare `worker` line,
# correct for the other two Dockerfiles (root Dockerfile / worker/Dockerfile)
# to keep their build contexts small, but wrong here: RunPod's GitHub-deploy
# build uses the repo root as context, and this Dockerfile needs files
# under worker/runpod-handler/ — the root ignore file would exclude them
# entirely. Confirmed empirically: handler.py's COPY failed as "not found"
# with the root .dockerignore in effect.
node_modules
.git
.next
.env*
docs
*.log
worker/models
